# NOTICE

## Provenance

The HLE host layer in `dm/host`, `dm/gfx/nvn` (the service side) and `dm/third_party`
originates from **[d2r-mobile](https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/d2r-mobile)** — the same
author's HarmonyOS-preceding iOS/macOS port of the Switch release of *Diablo II:
Resurrected*, published under the MIT licence.

What this repository adds, none of which exists upstream:

- `dm/ohos/` — the HarmonyOS port: NAPI module entry, XComponent surface, OHAudio
  renderer, touch/gamepad capture, the force-include compatibility layer, and the
  cross-build Makefile.
- `dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_vulkan.c` — an NVN→**Vulkan** replay layer (upstream replays into
  Metal). This is where the texture pack/upload chain, the shader program keying, and
  the presentation path live.
- `dm/host/hle_net.c` — rewritten from "always fail" to real BSD sockets, because the
  game's offline mode runs a dedicated server against `127.0.0.1` inside its own process.
- `dm/host/hle_fs.c` — the three-tier path resolution and the lazy basename index.
- `dm/host/hle_thread.c` — the pre-4.0 semaphore/condvar behaviour, the spurious-wake
  fallback, and the thread dumper.
- `dm/host/crash.c`, `dm/host/hle_svc.c`, `dm/host/diag.c` — the forensics work: crash
  scenes to file, hardened `Break` handling, per-thread last-SVC reporting.

The upstream MIT licence text and copyright notice are retained verbatim in
[LICENSE](LICENSE).

